# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DailyValue environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. `.env.local` is
# gitignored so your secrets never get committed.
#
# The app runs with NONE of these set — it falls back to a built-in engine and
# emoji tiles. Each key you add turns on a bit more. Restart `npm run dev`
# after editing, because these are only read when the server starts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- 1. Gemini — the primary brain -------------------------------------------
# Reads the shopper's sentence and returns the shopping list. This is the one
# that matters most: it is the only provider that can ENFORCE our JSON schema.
# Free key, no card: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional model override. Defaults to gemini-3.7-flash.
# Model names get retired. If searches suddenly fall back to Groq, check the
# server log - it prints the exact name Google wants instead. Set
# gemini-flash-latest here if you would rather never update this again.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.7-flash


# --- 2. Groq — the backup brain ----------------------------------------------
# Used ONLY when Gemini errors, times out, or runs out of daily quota. A
# different company on different hardware, so it is a genuinely independent
# point of failure.
# Free key, no card: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional model override. Defaults to openai/gpt-oss-120b.
# Groq has dropped Llama chat models entirely. Run `npm run check-keys` and it
# reports how many models your key can see.
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b


# --- 3. Pexels — product photos ----------------------------------------------
# Supplies a photo for products the AI generated, which have no image in
# /public. Without it, those cards fall back to an emoji tile.
# 200 requests/hour, 20,000/month. Instant approval: https://www.pexels.com/api/
PEXELS_API_KEY=
